From 11032898a0ae13f74866cdcf2fe7d6a77e3cafaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: czoli1976 <czoli1976@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:08:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SadTest: fully initialize ref_ in SADTestBase16bit SRC_MAX

The SRC_MAX case zeroed only MAX_SB_SIZE (128) of the MAX_BLOCK_SIZE
(128x128 = 16384) elements that SetUp() allocates for ref_, so every
block wider than the initialized window compared src_ against
uninitialized heap. NEON/SADTestSubSample16bit then passed or failed
depending on what the allocator handed back -- it fails in a full
SvtAv1UnitTests run once earlier suites have dirtied the heap, and
passes when run filtered on a fresh heap.

The sibling REF_MAX, RANDOM and UNALIGN cases in the same function all
loop to MAX_BLOCK_SIZE, and the 8-bit SADTestBase::prepare_data() uses
MAX_REF_BLOCK_SIZE for its ref buffers, so this was a typo.

Deterministic before/after check, poisoning freed memory so the recycled
allocation is non-zero:

  MallocScribble=1 ./Bin/Release/SvtAv1UnitTests \
      --gtest_filter="NEON/SADTestSubSample16bit.*"

Fixes #2384
---
 test/SadTest.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/SadTest.cc b/test/SadTest.cc
index b3f394a6c..e5cc10566 100644
--- a/test/SadTest.cc
+++ b/test/SadTest.cc
@@ -1493,7 +1493,7 @@ class SADTestBase16bit : public ::testing::Test {
             for (int i = 0; i < MAX_BLOCK_SIZE; i++)
                 src_[i] = mask;
 
-            for (int i = 0; i < MAX_SB_SIZE; i++)
+            for (int i = 0; i < MAX_BLOCK_SIZE; i++)
                 ref_[i] = 0;
 
             break;
